e  to put up a resistance thankfully though  the crews detour away in time to thaw  her believing Luffy the most capable  among them to deal with the strange new  character but even he is no match firm  and with relative ease this naval higher  up leaves Luffy frozen and completely  outmatched it's like he wasn't even  really trying the ending of this arc  left me with a strange feeling over the  last 300 or so chapters Luffy has been  proving himself to be far more  formidable than anyone thought he was  and the people he's proven himself to  have been far more than just the  villains he's found himself up against  he shown himself to be a person people  can rely on when all the chips are down  primarily to his crew over a number of  instances various crew members have made  passing remarks regarding how they don't  need to worry about Luffy that he's more  than capable that he  at hand but in this arc are not just one  but two separate occasions Luffy would  have lost in dramatic fashion had he not  been lucky and so while this arc was  largely light-hearted there was a really  humanizing message at its core that  Luffy has his limits that Luffy can be  defeated and even though he might want  to save everyone Luffy might not be able  to and that's my biggest takeaway from  this arc before I move into water 7 next  week to say that I am extremely excited  to see what's to come in this story is  an understatement with the knowledge now  that the Maine Navy HQ is in the region  they're heading towards next and that  they are fully aware of what Luffy did  to crocodile I'm very interested to see  how this new dynamic works with the  straw hats and more specifically from a  narrative perspective as in this act we  have reminded that the Navy are in fact  individuals with good intentions they  unlike the rest of the villains we've  come up against thus far want to help  people to do good which matches Luffy's  philosophy and that's not even to  mention how da Flamingo and the other  warlords of the sea play into all of  this and I still have no idea what that  mysterious repairman in sky Pia was  doing or who he was  I'm thoroughly pumped to see what comes  next and I can't wait to review it for  you guys next week I'm tackling water 7  so wish me luck but that'll do it for  this video I've been totally not mark  I'll see you all next week and thank you  so much for watching
 

